1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:03,020
How To Get A Salary Raise.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:07,790
I have a question for you, have you ever been
in this situation?

3
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:09,670
You work really hard.

4
00:00:09,670 --> 00:00:15,300
You exceed expectations at work, and the responsibilities
assigned to you, even though are way beyond

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,630
the scope of your job description, you do
them with excellence anyways.

6
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:23,490
Yet you feel like you are underpaid and underappreciated.

7
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:27,260
So to compensate for this you feel like you
should think about asking your boss for a

8
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,449
pay raise.

9
00:00:28,449 --> 00:00:33,940
Yet asking for a pay raise is something many
employees are nervous about doing, but this

10
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:35,600
shouldn’t be the case.

11
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,149
Your employers have invested resources to
train you, and they rely on you to perform

12
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:44,670
crucial tasks that are essential to the success
of your organization.

13
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:50,139
So, you will be surprised that they are often
willing to listen when valuable employees

14
00:00:50,139 --> 00:00:52,229
ask for a salary raise.

15
00:00:52,229 --> 00:00:57,699
It takes time and resources to recruit and
train new talent into an organization as well

16
00:00:57,699 --> 00:01:01,430
as incorporating them into the culture of
the organization.

17
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:06,350
This is why employers are more often willing
to listen to salary demands by employees.

18
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:10,890
So this happens to be one of your biggest
leverages if done right.

19
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:15,729
Statistics also favor employees that take
the crucial step to demand a raise.

20
00:01:15,729 --> 00:01:20,740
According to a survey by Payscale – a data
and compensation software company, employees

21
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:26,369
who earn above $150,000 annually say they
received the amount they requested for 70%

22
00:01:26,369 --> 00:01:27,869
of the time.

23
00:01:27,869 --> 00:01:32,350
So in today’s video, we will outline an
actionable guide to help you get the pay raise

24
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:33,600
you deserve.

25
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:40,009
But before we begin, if you feel like you
deserve a pay rise, click that like button.

26
00:01:40,009 --> 00:01:44,140
And also, are you a subscriber? if not what
are you waiting for?

27
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:48,960
Tab the subscribe button and bell icon so
you never miss any of our videos.

28
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:51,100
Now let’s begin…

29
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:56,080
First of all, outline the reasons why you
believe you deserve a salary raise.

30
00:01:56,080 --> 00:02:00,069
Confidence in the value of your abilities,
work and achievements is the first step towards

31
00:02:00,069 --> 00:02:01,530
getting a pay raise.

32
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:05,999
You won’t be able to convince yourself or
your bosses if you can’t show that you deserve

33
00:02:05,999 --> 00:02:08,759
more than what you are currently getting.

34
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:14,260
Stop complaining about your salary without
taking the necessary steps to increase it.

35
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:18,330
You need to review the description of the
job you signed up for and identify the extra

36
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:22,530
responsibilities and tasks that were not mentioned
in the job description.

37
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:27,239
When you can show that your contribution exceeds
what is expected of someone in your position

38
00:02:27,239 --> 00:02:32,570
and that such contribution has been beneficial
to the company, then you have a case for a

39
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:34,260
salary increase.

40
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:36,709
A crucial factor is keeping records.

41
00:02:36,709 --> 00:02:41,870
Your employer is primarily concerned with
the effective running and growth of the organization.

42
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:45,299
Your long list of accomplishments won’t
be his priority.

43
00:02:45,299 --> 00:02:49,800
To have a fruitful conversation about a pay
raise, then you must have records showing

44
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:54,620
off your efforts exceeding your job description,
and how those efforts have helped the organization

45
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,790
thrive.

46
00:02:55,790 --> 00:02:56,970
2.

47
00:02:56,970 --> 00:02:59,060
Figure out the value of your skills.

48
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:03,670
You don’t go into salary negotiations without
having a clear idea of what you are worth.

49
00:03:03,670 --> 00:03:07,840
You need to research your industry and figure
out what other workers who occupy similar

50
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:12,270
positions and perform similar roles are earning
in other places.

51
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:16,560
You can check out surveys by Professional
organizations or recruitment firms, check

52
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:20,840
job boards and see what other employers are
offering.

53
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:25,719
Use online tools like Glassdoor, Know Your
Worth, etc. to do your research.

54
00:03:25,719 --> 00:03:30,189
You can even go on interviews just to see
what other organizations are offering.

55
00:03:30,189 --> 00:03:32,049
Another approach will be to look within.

56
00:03:32,049 --> 00:03:36,380
If you think your colleagues earn more than
you do in basic salary and compensation, figure

57
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:39,950
out smart ways to get them to reveal their
earnings to you.

58
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:43,099
When you do all of these, you will have a
definite idea of your worth, and you will

59
00:03:43,099 --> 00:03:46,680
be equipped with some of the leverage you
will need during that important salary raise

60
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,959
conversation.

61
00:03:47,959 --> 00:03:49,239
3.

62
00:03:49,239 --> 00:03:51,020
Settle On A Realistic Number.

63
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:54,290
When you are doing your research, you should
always have in mind that similar roles and

64
00:03:54,290 --> 00:03:58,470
responsibilities do not always equate to similar
income.

65
00:03:58,470 --> 00:04:01,819
Many factors influence the pay scale of companies.

66
00:04:01,819 --> 00:04:05,689
The nature of the industry, the degree of
importance of specific roles in different

67
00:04:05,689 --> 00:04:10,390
companies, bonus packages for unique tasks,
and regional differences in income can all

68
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:15,459
explain why workers who perform similar roles
in some companies earn a lot more than you

69
00:04:15,459 --> 00:04:16,459
do.

70
00:04:16,459 --> 00:04:18,550
This doesn’t mean you shouldn’t ask for
a pay raise.

71
00:04:18,550 --> 00:04:22,580
It means that you should value yourself in
relation to the average pay that other similar

72
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:25,720
employees in your industry and your company
receive.

73
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,720
You want to be reasonable.

74
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:31,200
You shouldn’t go for a low number, and you
should also avoid a number that is too high.

75
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:36,770
To get what you want, ask for any amount that
is about 15% above what you believe you are

76
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:37,770
worth.

77
00:04:37,770 --> 00:04:40,510
This is because your employer will negotiate
with you, and any number you mention will

78
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:43,010
likely be haggled to a lower price.

79
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:46,470
When you demand a higher amount and it is
brought down, it will probably fall within

80
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:49,250
the range of what you wanted in the first
place.

81
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:50,950
You must be reasonable.

82
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:54,970
Asking your employer to double your salary
or asking for a bogus increase in your wages

83
00:04:54,970 --> 00:04:58,480
could offend your employer and cost you your
job.

84
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,480
4.

85
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,390
Build Your Case For A Pay Raise.

86
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:04,460
If you are absolutely convinced that you should
be earning more.

87
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:08,880
First of all, you have to decide and settled
on a reasonable salary you believe you should

88
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,140
be earning.

89
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:13,780
Then the next step is to compile the evidence
you will need to convince your boss that you

90
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,070
deserve a salary increase.

91
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:19,540
You’ll then need to re-examine your past
projects and the tasks you carry out daily

92
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:20,840
for your employers.

93
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:24,710
Collate data that shows how you exceed the
scope of your job description and the quality

94
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:26,310
of your performance.

95
00:05:26,310 --> 00:05:30,320
Make a list of your qualifications and accomplishments,
and gather evidence that shows what workers

96
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:33,210
with similar skills are paid, and document
it.

97
00:05:33,210 --> 00:05:37,030
You should also add your awards and the accolades
you have received during your loyal service

98
00:05:37,030 --> 00:05:38,500
to your employers.

99
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:42,560
Combine all of these in a logical presentation
that will be used to show your employer why

100
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,240
you need more money.

101
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,240
5.

102
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:47,000
Be Prepared To Negotiate.

103
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,250
It’s not often that your boss will agree
to the number you came up with, so you must

104
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:53,000
be ready to negotiate.

105
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,180
You must be prepared to present your case
with confidence and clarity.

106
00:05:57,180 --> 00:06:00,890
Doing your homework by following the steps
outlined previously will make preparations

107
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:03,760
for negotiations very straightforward.

108
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:07,960
Also if you haven’t checked out our how
to negotiate video, you should look it up.

109
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:08,990
6.

110
00:06:08,990 --> 00:06:11,060
Have A Back-Up Plan For Rejection.

111
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:14,330
The fact that you are entitled to a salary
increase doesn’t mean your boss will see

112
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:15,410
it that way.

113
00:06:15,410 --> 00:06:18,950
It could also be that current budgetary constraints
will make it difficult for your employer to

114
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:20,750
meet your salary demands.

115
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:23,330
This means you must have an alternative plan.

116
00:06:23,330 --> 00:06:28,350
What will you ask for if your boss does acknowledge
that indeed you do deserve a salary increase

117
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:30,240
but cannot currently provide it?

118
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,240
What will you do?

119
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:35,650
So, if you can’t get the salary increase
you want right now, then outline other perks

120
00:06:35,650 --> 00:06:38,100
you can demand that will fill the void.

121
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:42,250
At the same time, you should wait for another
opportunity to increase your wages.

122
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:46,180
You can ask for extra vacation time, increased
investment in your training and development,

123
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:50,770
a title change, more allowance, and even the
right to telecommute if your job can be done

124
00:06:50,770 --> 00:06:51,990
from home.

125
00:06:51,990 --> 00:06:54,560
These are just some perks you can ask for.

126
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,560
7.

127
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,060
Know When To Ask For A Raise.

128
00:06:58,060 --> 00:07:01,230
Timing is crucial if you want to get anything
you want in life.

129
00:07:01,230 --> 00:07:05,740
The state of the company should determine
when you should ask for a salary increase.

130
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:10,130
If your organization is going through a period
of declining revenues or funding, and employees

131
00:07:10,130 --> 00:07:14,730
are being fired to cut costs, then that is
not a good time to ask for more money.

132
00:07:14,730 --> 00:07:17,970
The layoffs may be responsible for your increased
workload.

133
00:07:17,970 --> 00:07:22,390
Your salary hasn’t changed at all to reflect
that, it is still better to wait until when

134
00:07:22,390 --> 00:07:26,470
your organization has tackled its challenges
before asking for a pay raise.

135
00:07:26,470 --> 00:07:32,120
However, a good time to ask for a salary increase
will be when things are booming and your organization’s

136
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:36,910
budgetary plans show a desire to invest in
growth and employee development.

137
00:07:36,910 --> 00:07:40,910
You can pick any of the following events to
set a date to discuss a salary increase with

138
00:07:40,910 --> 00:07:41,910
your boss:

139
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:46,730
After the successful completion of an important
project, you initiated and completed to a

140
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:48,080
high standard.

141
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:52,020
It may just be a good time to ask for that
salary increase.

142
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:55,850
During an annual performance review – mainly
when you know you have contributed a lot to

143
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,450
the progress of the organization during the
year

144
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:02,550
And when your boss is in a good mood – this
is subjective, but you should know your boss

145
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:05,080
well enough to know when he is happy.

146
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,080
8.

147
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:08,420
Schedule A Convenient Meeting With Your Boss.

148
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:12,250
You don’t want to ambush your boss with
a rash demand for a salary increase.

149
00:08:12,250 --> 00:08:16,990
Your boss must be aware that the scheduled
meeting is to discuss your pay, and the meeting

150
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:23,140
must take place at a time when your boss is
relaxed and willing to listen to your demands.

151
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:26,290
This is why we stated that timing is essential.

152
00:08:26,290 --> 00:08:30,040
If revenues or funding are going up, then
your boss will be more willing to have a chat

153
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,360
about more money.

154
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:36,279
Also, make sure you have prepared your presentation
and that you are ready to negotiate.

155
00:08:36,279 --> 00:08:39,949
Carry your portfolio of documents that will
be used to present your case.

156
00:08:39,949 --> 00:08:45,500
Come prepared with a list of ideas and future
plans in your role as an employee of the organization.

157
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,580
9.

158
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:48,060
Ask Your Boss.

159
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:52,480
You should start the conversation positively
and let your boss know that you like working

160
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,839
for them.

161
00:08:53,839 --> 00:08:57,899
Outline how you have developed in your role
and move on to why you feel your responsibilities

162
00:08:57,899 --> 00:09:01,040
and qualifications deserve a better salary.

163
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:05,500
You need to show a firm grasp of your role
in the organization when explaining the contrasting

164
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:10,520
nature of the job you signed up for and what
the organization always demands from you.

165
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:15,089
You must display confidence in your abilities
and talk in the appropriate tone.

166
00:09:15,089 --> 00:09:19,690
Also, you must be very specific when answering
a question about the amount you want to be

167
00:09:19,690 --> 00:09:20,690
paid.

168
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:23,529
Hesitation will weaken your hand when negotiating.

169
00:09:23,529 --> 00:09:28,000
Provide evidence of the value of your skills
on the job market and let your employers know

170
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,689
when you want the new salary to take effect.

171
00:09:30,689 --> 00:09:34,699
Your boss will likely negotiate with you,
so use the plan you developed during your

172
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:39,420
preparations for negotiations to navigate
the back and forth process of agreeing to

173
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:42,160
a number that will satisfy both parties.

174
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:45,879
If your boss asks for time to think about
it, be patient, and don’t lose hope.

175
00:09:45,879 --> 00:09:50,990
And if you get an immediate positive response,
then show your gratitude and appreciation.

176
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:51,990
10.

177
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:53,990
Respond Positively To A Rejection.

178
00:09:53,990 --> 00:09:57,740
If your request for a pay raise is declined
due to budget constraints and you are happy

179
00:09:57,740 --> 00:10:01,889
to stick around until the money becomes available,
then this is the right time to put your back-up

180
00:10:01,889 --> 00:10:03,149
plan in motion.

181
00:10:03,149 --> 00:10:07,259
However, if your boss is not convinced that
you deserve a pay raise and no clear answer

182
00:10:07,259 --> 00:10:12,319
is given as to when you can expect one, then
you should consider getting another job.

183
00:10:12,319 --> 00:10:16,310
Getting a higher salary elsewhere is easier
when you are a new talent that the employer

184
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:21,000
desperately needs, provided you have the track
record and qualifications to match your salary

185
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,269
demands.

186
00:10:22,269 --> 00:10:24,300
Thank you guys so much for watching.

187
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,769
Please leave a comment below, I’d love to
hear your views and thoughts.

188
00:10:27,769 --> 00:10:32,699
Don’t forget to like this video, subscribe,
enable notifications and I will see you in

189
00:10:32,699 --> 00:10:32,970
the next one.

